            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0996" n="967" xml:id="pg967"/>

                <head>252. Backchannel Message From the President’s Assistant for National Security
                    Affairs (Kissinger) to the Head of the Strategic Arms Limitation Talks
                    Delegation in Helsinki (Smith)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d252-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Salzburg White House</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1972-05-21T16:30:00+00:00">May 21, 1972,
                    1630Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p> WTE 16. Subject: SLBM.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>We cannot accept 48 modern submarines as Soviet base point, if they insist
                        that this includes only Y class or newer. It is imperative for Congressional
                        reasons that there must be some retirement of H and G classes involved in
                        Soviet reaching level of 62. For this reason, Soviet base point should be
                        about 41–43, which corresponds to real situation.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>It is also imperative that total of 950 for Soviets includes modern
                        missiles no matter on what submarine they are deployed.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Phrasing in our proposals on procedures for dismantling and replacement
                        must be amended to permit us to lay keels of ULMS without having to destroy
                        Polaris.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>You should act on these points immediately; these instructions will also
                        follow through normal channels.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d252-f2"/>
                    </item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d252-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d252-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential Materials, Box 427, NSC Files,
                    Backchannel Files, Backchannel Messages, 1972, SALT. Top Secret; Eyes Only;
                    Flash.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d252-f2" n="2" xml:id="d252-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 89509, May 21, the Department transmitted these “supplementary SALT
                    instructions” to the delegation in Helsinki, noting that point 3 was consistent
                    with NSDM 167 which did not require the start of destruction or dismantling of
                    old launchers until the launch of the new submarine. (Ibid., RG 59, Central
                    Files 1970–73, DEF 18–3 FIN (HE)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
